{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790962274,"nonce":"TyhlqYHQDPSzSUdbTV98DLOAp18=","title":"LayoutTree cannot change a text node's content or font after creation","message":"A text node's TextMeasureContext lives in taffy's node context\n(`taffy: TaffyTree\u003cTextMeasureContext\u003e`, tree.rs:211; `create_text_node`\ncalls `new_leaf_with_context`, tree.rs:253). LayoutTree exposes no way to\nread or change it afterwards, so content, font size and font name are fixed\nat creation.\n\nConsequences:\n- PropertyId::TextContent is declared (property.rs:71) with\n  SideEffects::TEXT, but nothing writes it and `needs_text_remeasure` is read\n  nowhere outside property.rs. blinc_cn's button says as much\n  (button.rs:336-338): a bound label rebuilds its subtree via deps().\n- PropertyId::FontFamily has nowhere to go: RenderProps has no family field.\n  For layout the family is TextMeasureContext.font_name / generic_font.\n\nBlinc's own apps change text by rebuilding (renderer/build/diff.rs:41), so\nan in-place writer conflicts with nothing. Embedders that drive a LayoutTree\ndirectly (ashui's Haxe bindings) have no way to bind text at all.\n\nProposed, after tree.rs:258, no other file changes:\n\n    pub fn update_text(\u0026mut self, id: LayoutNodeId,\n                       f: impl FnOnce(\u0026mut TextMeasureContext)) -\u003e bool {\n        let Some(\u0026n) = self.node_map.get(id) else { return false };\n        let Some(ctx) = self.taffy.get_node_context_mut(n) else { return false };\n        f(ctx);\n        let _ = self.taffy.mark_dirty(n);\n        true\n    }\n    pub fn text_context(\u0026self, id: LayoutNodeId) -\u003e Option\u003c\u0026TextMeasureContext\u003e\n\ntaffy 0.6.3 provides get_node_context_mut (taffy_tree.rs:580, does not\ndirty) and mark_dirty (746, dirties ancestors too). Blinc keeps no content-\nkeyed measurement cache, so taffy's per-node cache is the only one to clear.\n\nCaveat: Blinc's non-wrapping Text is built with create_node and a fixed size\n(text.rs:625-639), not a context, so update_text returns false for it.","files":null}]}